# Ship checklist

Before finishing a task that touches site behavior or content loaders:

```bash
npm test
```

This runs production build (webpack) + `scripts/test-agentic.mjs` (starts server, checks routes, llms.txt, sitemap, markdown negotiation).

## When tests fail

- Homepage section renamed → update assertions in `scripts/test-agentic.mjs`
- New public route → add to `src/app/sitemap.ts` + agentic test loop + `src/proxy.ts` known paths if needed
- New gratitude person → `content/people/slug.mdx` (sitemap picks it up via `getAllPeople()`)
- New trust page → `content/pages/slug.mdx` + `pageSlugs` in `content-types.ts`
- Client bundle fs error → move loader to server page, pass props

## Git

- Commit only when user asks
- Do not commit `.env.local`, secrets, or dev-only `next-env.d.ts` path churn from local `next dev`
- Keep the Next.js block in `AGENTS.md` (regenerated by `next dev`)

## Scope discipline

- Content change → usually 1–3 markdown files
- UI polish → match existing `ink-link`, `site-shell`, section spacing
- Avoid drive-by refactors unrelated to the request
